A plain compile does not run BibTeX or biber. Use **References › Update Bibliography**, which compiles with a real bibliography pass and extra runs.

If it still shows `[?]`, check that:

- the key in `\cite{key}` matches an entry in your `.bib` file exactly (case matters);
- the document contains `\bibliography{…}` (BibTeX) or `\printbibliography` (biblatex);
- the `.bib` file is inside the project folder and spelled correctly.

The message after the update names the tool used and lists any warnings.
